time you know people  couldn't  go out of their homes to work a lot of  people were starting to go hungry  and so we kind of used some of the  resources we had to  start sending bitcoin to the majority of  the families in el zante and teaching  the stores how to accept  bitcoin which helped the the stores to  be able to you know stay in business and  keep their employees  on but it also allowed the the people to  remain  fed maria del carmen the owner of a tiny  pizza eatery  says she was skeptical about storing  money on her phone  now bitcoin accounts for as much as half  of her roughly 45 dollars a day in sales  sienna  enzo rubio owner of breakpoint cafe  never thought twice about crypto until  his customers asked him about it  within the first week of his opening and  he showed me the app  we downloaded it in three minutes i had  the app  the wallet in my phone and he paid me  my first cappuccino on bitcoin  shops in town price everything in  dollars whether the underlying  transaction is in bitcoin or not  a cappuccino always costs and fifty  cents  even if bitcoin's value has just jumped  or dropped in this way  it behaves more like a token than a  currency  what was in my mind at that point was  what am i going to do with it am i  losing my money  did i give coffee for free and now  whatever i get on bitcoin is i keep it  as savings  that brings a risk of volatility into  play since mid-april bitcoin has lost  nearly half of its value  and the international monetary fund has  warned that crypto assets can post  significant risks  mike's team is preparing residents for  an extended down cycle by moving some  holdings into us dollars  or making large purchases now while  prices are high  obviously bitcoin has been trending up  during the time of this you know the  project  and we understand that might not always  be the case but we found that people  actually  they learn really quickly how to ride  volatility how  to adjust how to think you know which  funds  am i putting aside for 10 years where  i'm not really worried about it  which funds are for next week so i need  to move it into dollars to be able to  make a dollar denominated payment  and it's actually been much less of an  issue than we initially anticipated  although locals were skeptical at first  many feel saved by the implementation of  crypto in their community  a  el salvador's bitcoin law will come into  effect on september 7th  [Music]


